From: Dynamic Devices <engineering@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] Use compatible C++20 spelling for native build

GCC 10 supports C++20 as -std=gnu++2a but rejects -std=gnu++20.
The spelling selects the same dialect and lets the Foundries native host
compiler build Node 22's host tools.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Foundries host toolchain compatibility]

diff --git a/common_node.gypi b/common_node.gypi
index 590d932..bc9600a 100644
--- a/common_node.gypi
+++ b/common_node.gypi
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
       # Override common.gypi config to use C++20 for Node.js core only.
       ['OS in "linux freebsd openbsd solaris android aix os400 cloudabi"', {
         'cflags_cc!': ['-std=gnu++17'],
-        'cflags_cc': ['-std=gnu++20'],
+        'cflags_cc': ['-std=gnu++2a'],
       }],
       ['OS=="mac" and clang==1', {
         'xcode_settings': {
